  "type": "reading",
  "title": "Passage Two · Children’s Dreams",
  "subtitle": "婴幼儿的梦境与快速眼动睡眠",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "source": "2025年12月大学英语四级考试真题（第2套）· Section C · Passage Two",
  "instructions": "Questions 51 to 55 are based on the following passage.",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "en": "Adults dream during REM (rapid eye movement) sleep and infants have loads of REM. So, it might be fair to assume that babies have tons of dreams.",
      "zh": "成年人会在快速眼动（REM）睡眠期间做梦，而婴儿有大量的快速眼动睡眠。因此，似乎有理由推测婴儿也会做很多梦。"
    },
    {
      "en": "But scientists believe REM serves a completely different purpose for newborns and infants than dreaming. When babies are in REM, it allows their brain to develop pathways, connections, and eventually, learn languages.",
      "zh": "但科学家认为，快速眼动睡眠对新生儿和婴儿发挥着与做梦完全不同的作用。婴儿处于快速眼动睡眠时，这一状态有助于大脑形成神经通路和连接，并最终学习语言。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Since your baby doesn’t dream at this stage of brain development, it’s safe to assume babies do not have nightmares, either. Nightmares stem from exposure to trauma (创伤), an overactive imagination, and the normal stresses of everyday life.",
      "zh": "既然宝宝在大脑发育的这一阶段不会做梦，那么可以合理推断，婴儿也不会做噩梦。噩梦源于遭受创伤、想象力过度活跃，以及日常生活中的一般压力。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Are you wondering, what do babies dream about? Good question, but the answer is nothing!",
      "zh": "你是否好奇，婴儿会梦见什么？这个问题问得好，但答案是：什么也不会梦见！"
    },
    {
      "en": "So, when do babies start dreaming? The general consensus is that they start dreaming around the age of two. Psychologist David Foulkes studies children (from very small kids to teens) to bring the secrets of their dreams to the light of day. In his lab, he lets kids fall asleep and then wakes them 3 times a night and asks them to describe what they recall.",
      "zh": "那么，婴儿什么时候开始做梦呢？普遍共识是，他们大约在两岁时开始做梦。心理学家戴维·福克斯研究从低龄幼儿到青少年的儿童，以揭开他们梦境的奥秘。在实验室里，他让孩子们入睡，然后每晚叫醒他们3次，请他们描述能回忆起的梦境。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Foulkes’ findings are unsurprising. Basically, little kids have little dreams. But exactly what kids see while dreaming depends on their age. As children develop and grow, their dreams do too.",
      "zh": "福克斯的研究结果并不令人意外。基本上，年幼孩子的梦境较为简单。但儿童在梦中具体看到什么，取决于他们的年龄。随着儿童发育和成长，他们的梦境也会随之发展。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Dreams of very small kids are usually just snapshots (快照), looking much more like a slideshow than a movie, when compared to the dreams of adults. They heavily feature animals and other familiar sights, like images of people eating. According to Foulkes, “Children’s dream life ... seems to be similar to their waking imagination and narration.” Kids ages 5-9 begin seeing moving images and characters in action. Dreams now include multiple events strung together, one after the other. They also start developing greater ability to remember dreams. Still, that’s not always the case: When roused during REM sleep, 25% of the kids in Foulkes’ studies had no recollection of dreaming, a trend that continues through age 9.",
      "zh": "与成年人如同电影般的梦境相比，低龄儿童的梦通常只是片段式的快照，更像幻灯片放映。梦中经常出现动物和其他熟悉的场景，例如人们吃饭的画面。福克斯说：“儿童的梦境世界……似乎与他们清醒时的想象和叙事相似。”5至9岁的儿童开始在梦中看到动态画面和活动的人物。此时梦境会包含多个依次串联的事件。他们记住梦境的能力也开始增强。不过，情况并非总是如此：在福克斯的研究中，25%的儿童在快速眼动睡眠期间被唤醒时，完全不记得自己做过梦，这种现象一直持续到9岁。"
    },
    {
      "en": "So, if your baby seems to be in a stressful state while sleeping or is upset upon waking, there may be other factors at play.",
      "zh": "因此，如果宝宝睡觉时看起来紧张，或醒来后烦躁不安，可能是其他因素在起作用。"
    }
  ],
